<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bombed factories, billion-dollar opportunity: Why German companies are staying in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:209d7a44371e2ca020afa1547a2eb406bb414245469c273f05042725fa06afc2</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T11:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201--13f674deb921.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bombed-factories-billion-dollar-opportunity-why-german-companies-are-staying-in-ukraine/a-80030201?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German companies remain committed to Ukraine despite million-dollar losses, an unreliable energy supply and a shortage of skilled workers. They are betting on new markets and long-term growth.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Wadephul 'shocked' by Trump's Nvidia intervention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15055c4c71dccd5bfa7a21777cc0cf76edfbf807990212062314ec170851aa92</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T13:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-shocked-by-trump-s-nvidia-intervention/a-80033954--71b26658a53e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-shocked-by-trump-s-nvidia-intervention/a-80033954?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German foreign minister has criticized Donald Trump's interference in the chip-maker's economic activities. Jensen Huang was brought back after stepping down as Nvidia CEO amid multiple scandals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU imposes import quotas for hybrid vehicles from China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bc9425cfb2cb4fb675fe7807122ce1059a4b927c0eb6e486cc240401f77ef04</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981--7d148967ab4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is trying to protect its own car manufacturers from what it called "overcapacity" in China. Carmakers in the bloc, especially in Germany, have been lagging behind their Chinese rivals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen begins wage talks with IG Metall union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76e1ada2aa9fda5639b0a78815760b787529f1342e753b6b3dfc6ba18375cdc4</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-begins-wage-talks-with-ig-metall-union/live-80028306--34d90226a697.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-begins-wage-talks-with-ig-metall-union/live-80028306?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's largest labor union IG Metall and automaker Volkswagen are holding wage negotiations, as the company looks to embark on cost-cutting measures. Meanwhile, Germany's president is in Ghana. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police respond to multiple school bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33ee526343e1ae3b0943293f06e035fa87f4494698b6d9d38ef9b9410110863b</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842--56ba1301d92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in Germany are responding to bomb threats against a series of schools, but say that at present they don't believe them to be credible. Danish authorities are reporting a similar series of apparent hoaxes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NATO Parliamentary Assembly convenes amid Russian airspace violations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff9af9341b8fefea977b1eb896034f9135cf0217335867b736dde94909cf3125</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T09:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nato-parliamentary-assembly-convenes-amid-russian-airspace-violations/live-80016415--9a53102043ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nato-parliamentary-assembly-convenes-amid-russian-airspace-violations/live-80016415?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy and German Foreign Minister Wadephul are set to address the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin while NATO representatives discuss Russian airspace violations in Brussels. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Metalworkers go on strike as pay dispute heats up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c775cc2ecd69c0c8a8febe2b6c81a482b590b41aaa8fbdcad17c49eae46251c</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633--a1790c046188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-metalworkers-go-on-strike-as-pay-dispute-heats-up/live-80015633?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's biggest union is calling for more strikes over heated pay disputes with car makers like Mercedes and shipyards among the companies impacted. Meanwhile, a Berlin hospital fire leaves many injured.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d92f110b4ed743d5415d6b0f99b22f2d6a1ea679327a3952385d59a6ee586c8</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German directors' doc on stolen film wins International Emmy Award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ec8b9760b835a15e3aec136ef2da94fd744f00510544c0ea78071bdc588eea8</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455--80792ca0c998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-directors-doc-on-stolen-film-wins-international-emmy-award/a-76103455?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two German film students confronted the American who won festival prizes with their animated movie. "The Talented Mr. F," their documentary on their fight against plagiarism, is now in the spotlight.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Weapons, war and wavering trust: Germans want to see more restraint in foreign policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e47d1ec9a1a1cf757e7542dcc5882d2d87b0379ab4889883794a98e4be2d507d</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254--66b3f174435c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a study by the Körber Foundation, a growing number of Germans now oppose providing military aid to Ukraine. The majority also believes that Germany should take a neutral position between the US and China.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a516151866247077fdeae5b11478785fcf04d17c193bd7a110c6a28ce5a20aa6</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Budget cuts threaten Germany's fight against antisemitism and racism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23f05a909dfe60a300603ecf01fb1538449c0c8fc9a74184afa6cccff0834cb0</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644--fcf379d5b1d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/budget-cuts-threaten-germany-s-fight-against-antisemitism-and-racism/a-80018644?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Numerous grassroots initiatives in Germany are facing funding cuts. Affected organizations are sounding the alarm, pointing to growing challenges posed by far-right extremism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6dcac703ee114ca2c514fd6c279d73bdb58614773c4b69b94d89e123100b74</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
